==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|lexically}} {{IPA|en|/ʌɣ/|/ʌ(ɡ)/|/ʌx/|/əː/}}
* {{q|natural exclamation}} Any low-back vowel followed by a fricative articulated between the velum and the throat.
**Note: may be [[w:nasalization|nasalized]].
* {{audio|en|en-us-ugh.ogg|a=US}} , {{audio|en|en-us-ugh-2.ogg|a=US}} , {{audio|en|en-us-ugh-3.ogg|a=US}}

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{n-g|Used to express [[repugnance]], [[disgust]], or [[annoyance]].}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:yuck}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Ugh'''! The bread in the pantry has gone moldy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1855|author=w:Robert Browning|title=s:Childe Roland to the Dark Tower Came|section=XXI
|passage=[...] It may have been a water-rat I speared, / But, '''ugh'''! it sounded like a baby's shriek.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1886|translator=H.L. Br&aelig;kstad|author=w:Peter Christen Asbjørnsen|title=Folk and Fairy Tales|page=57|passage="'''Ugh,''' what a smell of Christian blood there is here," screamed the giant.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Paint The Town Red|artist=w:Doja Cat|year=2023|album=Scarlet|passage='''Ugh''', you can't take that bitch nowhere}}
# {{n-g|Used to express inarticulate vocalisations, such as used by a caveman.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1921|year_published=1958|author=[[w:H. G. Wells|H.G. Wells]]|chapter=The Grisly Folk|title=Selected Short Stories|page=291|passage=The brothers surveyed the wide prospect earnestly. "'''Ugh'''!" said one abruptly and pointed. "'''Ugh'''!" cried his brother. The eyes of the whole tribe swung round to the pointing finger. The group became one rigid stare.}}

